{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974068-some-dominate-devotions","id":974068,"title":"Some Dominate Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T15:37:36-07:00","id":974068,"title":"Some Dominate Devotions","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stepford Grin (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Majesty \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar64_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"64\" data-vbnamecard=\"64\">figurehead</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/88683-new-devotion-stepford\">Stepford</a> Devotion)</span><br /> <br /> Normally, Dominate is incapable of dictating what someone <i>feels</i> about a situation. You can't order someone to like the dress you're wearing, or make them love the son you just fabricated. Majesty, on the other hand, is all about playing people's emotions like a penny-whistle. When you combine the two, you can pretty much edit people's heads as much as you like.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> +1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> Stepford Grin enhances any Dominate power you might use, allowing you to give orders relating to emotions. When so enhanced, you can use Mesmerize to give more abstract commands relating to emotional reactions, could use Iron Edict to reduce someone to a useless sobbing wreck for the night, or could use The Lying Mind to turn their love for their spouse into bitter hatred.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Cost:</b> This Devotion costs 3xp to learn.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Command the Soulless (Dominate \u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> A human's soul insulates them from certain amounts of mental manipulation. Of course, in it's absence, a clever predator can slip their words in like hooks. This Devotion is rare amongst Kindred - after all, the most common users happen to be Strix.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Permanent<br /> <br /> You gain a +2 bonus when using Dominate on characters with the Soulless condition. In addition, you treat characters with the Enervated condition as if they had the Subservient condition, and characters with the Thrall condition as if they had the Enslaved condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Cost:</b> This Devotion costs 1xp to learn.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seed of the Hive (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> Particularly potent Kindred can leave &quot;shards&quot; of their mind in victims, allowing them to command them wordlessly. It has some... side effects, surely, but it's still rather effective for what it does.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae, 1 Willpower dot<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> You may spend one Willpower dot while forcing a Mesmerized victim to imbibe your blood (which carries all the normal effects of drinking Vitae). Doing so allows you to speak telepathically to your meat puppets, as long as they are within 10 yards per dot of Blood Potency of you. In addition to the obvious benefit of doing so, this allows you to bypass any language barrier when giving commands.<br /> <br /> If multiple victims of this Devotion are capable of seeing each-other, they can broadcast short, concrete statements to each-other telepathically. More insidiously, they can apply their Defence against surprise attacks unless <i>all</i> of the other victims of the Devotion they can see would also be blindsided by the attack.<br /> <br /> You regain any Willpower dots spend on this Devotion when the Mesmerized condition lapses.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Cost:</b> This Devotion costs 3xp to learn.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <b>Conditioning</b> + <b>Stepford Grin</b> = Essentially figurehead's Stepford Devotion. Sadly, it still doesn't replace them with robots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 09-21-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:54:09-07:00","id":974079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974068-some-dominate-devotions#post974068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stepford Grin (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Majesty \u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar64_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"64\" data-vbnamecard=\"64\">figurehead</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/88683-new-devotion-stepford\">Stepford</a> Devotion)</span><br /> <br /> Normally, Dominate is incapable of dictating what someone <i>feels</i> about a situation. You can't order someone to like the dress you're wearing, or make them love the son you just fabricated. Majesty, on the other hand, is all about playing people's emotions like a penny-whistle. When you combine the two, you can pretty much edit people's heads as much as you like.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> +1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> Stepford Grin enhances any Dominate power you might use, allowing you to give orders relating to emotions. When so enhanced, you can use Mesmerize to give more abstract commands relating to emotional reactions, could use Iron Edict to reduce someone to a useless sobbing wreck for the night, or could use The Lying Mind to turn their love for their spouse into bitter hatred.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Cost:</b> This Devotion costs 2xp to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Majesty 3 does this already.<br /> This: give more abstract commands relating to emotional reactions, could use Iron Edict to reduce someone to a useless sobbing wreck for the night, or could use The Lying Mind to turn their love for their spouse into bitter hatred.<br /> <br /> Majesty 3 shifts emotions.<br /> Lying Mind could already potentially make someone hate someone else. You would rewrite their memories to believe something that wasnt true and it could lead to hate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974068-some-dominate-devotions#post974068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seed of the Hive (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> Particularly potent Kindred can leave &quot;shards&quot; of their mind in victims, allowing them to command them wordlessly. It has some... side effects, surely, but it's still rather effective for what it does.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae, 1 Willpower dot<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> You may spend one Willpower dot while forcing a Mesmerized victim to imbibe your blood (which carries all the normal effects of drinking Vitae). Doing so allows you to speak telepathically to your meat puppets, as long as they are within 10 yards per dot of Blood Potency of you. In addition to the obvious benefit of doing so, this allows you to bypass any language barrier when giving commands.<br /> <br /> If multiple victims of this Devotion are capable of seeing each-other, they can broadcast short, concrete statements to each-other telepathically. More insidiously, they can apply their Defence against surprise attacks unless <i>all</i> of the other victims of the Devotion they can see would also be blindsided by the attack.<br /> <br /> You regain any Willpower dots spend on this Devotion when the Mesmerized condition lapses.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Cost:</b> This Devotion costs 3xp to learn.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex 4 gives you telepathy. And you can already dominate someone to drink your blood with dot 1. However, overcoming the language barrier is a nice touch. I would say this should be Auspex 4 and Dominate 1 and 2 experience<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am not a fan of giving devotions that can already be done with another discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-21-2016, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:15:39-07:00","id":974200,"title":"","content":"Stepford Grin...<br /> <br /> 1) <i>Really</i> speeds up long-term emotion editing with The Lying Mind. Compare making someone hate their spouse by coming up with a bunch of fake bad memories, and doing so by saying &quot;you hate your spouse because they forgot your birthday.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Unlike doing things the long way with The Lying Mind, you can cause entirely inappropriate emotional responses, like &quot;you were ecstatic at your daughter's funeral&quot; or &quot;your sister's smile has always terrified you&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3) Allows you to dictate an emotional response to something, while Majesty 3 just lets you set their emotional state. These aren't the same thing.<br /> <br /> Though, looking back... it should be Dominate 4 Majesty 3. I'll fix that.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> I'm running Seed of the Hive off of Dominate 5 (shove your mind inside other people) rather than Auspex 4 (read people's minds) because Seed of the Hive is purely one-way on your part (note it says 'speak to', not 'speak with' ). Plus, the &quot;make them drink the vitae&quot; thing is part of the Devotion's <i>cost</i>, not the effect.<br /> <br /> The second paragraph is a raw thrall-buff, which is Dominate territory.<br /> <br /> Both Seed of the Hive and Lay Open The Mind have different uses:<br /> <br /> <b>They both</b> let you broadcast thoughts to someone else.<br /> <b>Seed of the Hive</b> enhances your thralls, and removes the language barrier when commanding your thralls.<br /> <b>Lay Open The Mind</b> lets you hear their thoughts too, and lets you drag up and view memories.<br /> <br /> Lay Open The Mind is <i>much</i> better when it comes to being telepathy for telepathy's sake - Seed of the Hive is there for when you want to play Paxton Fettel.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not a fan of giving devotions that can already be done with another discipline. </div> </div> </div>[Insert snide comment that indicates that I'm kinda annoyed that you added this line, since it sounds pretty condescending.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:24:44-07:00","id":974206,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I saw Seed of the Hive, and thought it would end up being a Mind Seed (D&amp;D 3.5 Psionic power) like effect - You replace their mind with a copy of your own (eventually).<br /> <br /> What would that look like? I mean, they'd only think they were you - their capabilities would remain the same, be it human, Ghoul, other Vampire, or other being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:08:15-07:00","id":974485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974068-some-dominate-devotions#post974068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stepford Grin (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Majesty \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar64_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"64\" data-vbnamecard=\"64\">figurehead</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-