></div> </div> </div> </div>Love, love, love this Devotion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974068-some-dominate-devotions#post974068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seed of the Hive (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022)</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Particularly potent Kindred can leave &quot;shards&quot; of their mind in victims, allowing them to command them wordlessly. It has some... side effects, surely, but it's still rather effective for what it does.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae, 1 Willpower dot<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> You may spend one Willpower dot while forcing a Mesmerized victim to imbibe your blood (which carries all the normal effects of drinking Vitae). Doing so allows you to speak telepathically to your meat puppets, as long as they are within 10 yards per dot of Blood Potency of you. In addition to the obvious benefit of doing so, this allows you to bypass any language barrier when giving commands.<br /> <br /> If multiple victims of this Devotion are capable of seeing each-other, they can broadcast short, concrete statements to each-other telepathically. More insidiously, they can apply their Defence against surprise attacks unless <i>all</i> of the other victims of the Devotion they can see would also be blindsided by the attack.<br /> <br /> You regain any Willpower dots spend on this Devotion when the Mesmerized condition lapses.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Cost:</b> This Devotion costs 3xp to learn.<br /> <br /> =---=</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Seem to much better fits Dominate + Voivode Coil Devotion instead of Vigor. Also I'd remove the Willpower Dot Regain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:29:02-07:00","id":974555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974068-some-dominate-devotions?p=974200#post974200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stepford Grin...<br /> <br /> 1) <i>Really</i> speeds up long-term emotion editing with The Lying Mind. Compare making someone hate their spouse by coming up with a bunch of fake bad memories, and doing so by saying &quot;you hate your spouse because they forgot your birthday.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Unlike doing things the long way with The Lying Mind, you can cause entirely inappropriate emotional responses, like &quot;you were ecstatic at your daughter's funeral&quot; or &quot;your sister's smile has always terrified you&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3) Allows you to dictate an emotional response to something, while Majesty 3 just lets you set their emotional state. These aren't the same thing.<br /> <br /> Though, looking back... it should be Dominate 4 Majesty 3. I'll fix that.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> I'm running Seed of the Hive off of Dominate 5 (shove your mind inside other people) rather than Auspex 4 (read people's minds) because Seed of the Hive is purely one-way on your part (note it says 'speak to', not 'speak with' ). Plus, the &quot;make them drink the vitae&quot; thing is part of the Devotion's <i>cost</i>, not the effect.<br /> <br /> The second paragraph is a raw thrall-buff, which is Dominate territory.<br /> <br /> Both Seed of the Hive and Lay Open The Mind have different uses:<br /> <br /> <b>They both</b> let you broadcast thoughts to someone else.<br /> <b>Seed of the Hive</b> enhances your thralls, and removes the language barrier when commanding your thralls.<br /> <b>Lay Open The Mind</b> lets you hear their thoughts too, and lets you drag up and view memories.<br /> <br /> Lay Open The Mind is <i>much</i> better when it comes to being telepathy for telepathy's sake - Seed of the Hive is there for when you want to play Paxton Fettel.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [Insert snide comment that indicates that I'm kinda annoyed that you added this line, since it sounds pretty condescending.]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First, I am sorry If I came off as condescending. I apologize. Perhaps I am a little jaded as so many people come to these forums looking for validation and not actual help and I probably took that out on you. I am sorry. But what you want done can be done with things that already exist. At least for the two I posted. <br /> <br /> Sure the lying mind takes a couple of minutes and if all you want is to do it &quot;Faster&quot; then dominate 4 and Celerity 1 and it can cut that time down to nothing. <br /> <br /> &quot;When changing memories or creating new ones, the vampire can create the factual content of the memory but the victim's thoughts and feelings remain out of her control. She can create an environment that makes him predisposed to certain reactions, but she cant force him to love a son she has just invented.&quot;<br /> <br /> You want to make someone hate their wife, give them a ton of false memories of their wife cheating on them, stealing boozing, whatever. The man will hate his wife, feel betrayed, remember that betrayal ect.<br /> <br /> If you want the person to remember that they were totally ecstatic at their daughter's funeral, that is totally within the purview of the power. Just add a little bit on Why they were ecstatic, they remember these things as facts, that they were totally real. <br /> <br /> Now if you wanted to give a false memory and create a son that doesnt exist, you totally can, But if you want that son to be loved with all their heart, that is Majesty. Majesty setting it and dictating it are pretty much the same thing. Both are you chosing the emotional response. Are they so painfully depressed they dont want to live? That is you setting it and you dictating that they are depressed.<br /> <br /> Just recently someone wanted to make a nightmare devotion that gave them all the abilities of Protean. My perception of the situation seemed to be that people did not think it was right for a devotion of Nightmare to do something Protean does. This is nearly the same thing. You still need Dominate and Majesty to get this done, but you don't need to dump extra exp into it, because it's possible without the devotion. If you want it done faster, in say a turn, make a devotion with celerity. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for your second point. Auspex 4 allows you to &quot;Project thoughts, either by speaking directly into the victim's thoughts or depositing a mental image or memory&quot; You dont need words to convey your meaning. Which would also transcend the language barrier. If you want them to run out to the car and grab something, you send them the imagery of doing so. It allows you to hear their thoughts and implant small memories... it is literally everything you want to do with this power save connecting everyone's minds.<br /> <br /> If you want to link people's minds with telepathy so they can all see each other to give some sort of blind sense to everyone near by that would be Auspex + Vigor devotion to make it stronger. <br /> <br /> Possession is not controlling their mind. it is controlling their body. You go inside them and use them as a meat suit, they are no longer home for the time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:28:11-07:00","id":976406,"title":"","content":"A devotion which no cost and as a permanent effect? That doesn't seem right, at all. Why not increase the effect and throw a vitae cost on it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}